  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Services for Assisted Passage, Medical and Related Services for Australian Government Funded Refugees and Special Humanitarian Program Entrants</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this project, IOM aims to arrange the safe, orderly and dignified movement of refugees and other vulnerable persons to Australia while ensuring the highest standards of assistance is provided to the beneficiaries being resettled to Australia. Particularly, IOM is facilitating the visa/travel document processing in Lebanon and Turkey, providing health assessments and pre-embarkation checks to establish fitness to travel, as well as providing movement management and support to the final destination.</narrative>
  </description>
